      "description": "Edwards Sanborn Solar + Storage is Axium Infrastructure's manager-level holding across the operating EdSan 1A and EdSan 1B utility-scale solar and battery-storage phases in Kern County, California. Axium's current portfolio reports 346 MW of solar and 1,339 MWh of storage for 1A and 358 MW of solar and 1,497 MWh of storage for 1B, while the transaction releases disclose 397 MWac / 1,505 MWh and 410 MWac / 1,497 MWh nameplate figures respectively. The projects serve utility, municipal-utility and corporate counterparties under long-term revenue contracts. Phase 1A closed with Axium at 80% and Terra-Gen at 20%; Phase 1B closed with Axium ES Holdings at 50% and Terra-Gen at 50%. AxInfra US LP owns 92.26% of Axium Co-Invest Holdings, the upstream co-invest holding company. No synthetic combined-company ownership percentage is inferred, no direct source identifies AxInfra Fund I-IV as the owning fund, and no later Axium sale or signed pending exit was identified through August 18, 2026.",
